rf-story\">As of Oct 12, July to August is the driest pair on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids at 1.70 inches of normal, and it came in under 90% of normal in 37 of the 75 years since 1951. On the middle of the grids, June to July hit 24% of normal in 2025. Every grid had its driest year in 1952, with grid 33331 lowest at 61%. The preliminary estimate on grid 33331 puts July to August 2026 at 42.4, an estimate from NOAA rain that RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ from.</p>"}
